00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:37.180
Another new, interesting member, huh?

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:43.840
Please let Teio and McQueen have great races!

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.370
And then, please, make this my year!

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.120
<i>Help me make Spica the best team.</i>

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:50.070
With more shops all over the campus, 
and merch stands at the race tracks,

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.830
<i>I will </i>not<i> lose to her!</i>

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.160
<i>I want to win the Dream Trophy.</i>

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:54.410
leading into online sales, so that 
I can ultimately expand overseas and...

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.350
<i>I also have a wish from Suzuka-san.</i>

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:56.510
<i>Safety first...</i>

00:03:56.510 --> 00:04:00.200
<i>For the honor of the Mejiro family, 
I must win a successive spring Tennoushou.</i>

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.770
I'm gonna be an undefeated horse girl!

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.650
You're not supposed to shout your prayers.

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:20.360
Okay!

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:28.280
Looking good, Teio!

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:33.250
It all starts here, Teio.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.800
Look at her kick it up!

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.890
I didn't think she'd be in 
this kind of shape so soon.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.060
Hell, she might be better than ever.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.070
<i>Just watch me, Prez!</i>

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.820
<i>I'm gonna make a comeback!</i>

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.570
Trainer-san!

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:09.530
<b>Hayakawa
Tazuna</b>

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.650
Tazuna-san? What's wrong?

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:16.920
It's amazing! Teio-san and McQueen-san 
have been selected for the URA Awards!

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.730
You guys, that's amazing!

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:26.300
We will now be awarding the 
final URA Awards of the year.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.930
On stage to receive them are 
these two young ladies.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.230
While she unfortunately missed her chance 
at the Triple Crown, with 134 votes,

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:37.380
she has been selected as 
Horse Girl of the Year: Tokai Teio-san!

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.690
Yeah!

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.940
Congratulations.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:44.100
Although I'm sure there were 
a few pity votes included.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.620
Say what?

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:49.700
Including the Spring Tennoushou, she's won 
three races and come in second twice,

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.230
a remarkable record.

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:53.950
She has been selected as 
Top Senior-Class Horse Girl of the Year.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:55.590
Mejiro McQueen-san!

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:57.480
This is such an honor.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.210
That's McQueen for you.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.510
Shame about the Arima Kinen, though.

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:02.920
What was that?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:06.300
Can you two not just give 
sincere compliments?

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.550
Could the two of you give us a 
few words about your upcoming goals?

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.100
My goal's to be undefeated!

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.680
I intend to win a second 
consecutive Spring Tennoushou!

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:23.480
To reflect their accomplishments, they are 
both being provided with new racing wear.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.570
Awesome!

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:25.770
Thank you very much.

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:29.030
Everyone is going to be looking forward 
to your performances this year!

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.150
Let's give them a big round of applause!

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:37.830
Who do you think would win if they raced?

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.580
Teio, probably.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.750
Nah, I think it'd be McQueen.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:44.210
Makes you wanna see how it'd turn out.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.510
We may even see these two compete 
against each other, this year.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.720
<b>URA AWARD WINNERS NAMED!</b>

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.000
Wow, Spica!

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.900
I guess Spica's the top team now.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:02.010
Meanwhile, our team is...

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:04.640
We keep coming close, but...

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.980
Doesn't that bug you, trainer?!

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:11.610
I'd say it does. It'd be wonderful if 
we could prove what we were capable of.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.800
I say Canopus' goal is to beat Spica!

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.360
I don't think that's—

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.400
An excellent objective.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:18.950
Down with Spica!

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.300
Here we go!

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:21.560
Yeah!

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.580
Yeah?

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:25.340
Time to declare war on Spica!

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.870
Down with Spica!

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:30.410
Down with Spica!

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.590
Wouldn't it be better to train?

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.680
<b>Spica</b>

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:36.680
Looks like everyone is 
gunning for Spica this year.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:40.470
Everyone's gonna be coming 
at us, so stay on your toes.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.020
The letter arrow worked perfectly!

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.440
Retreat!

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:47.440
Run away!

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:47.440
Why did I come along?

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.120
Trainer! They shot a letter arrow at us!

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:51.580
What?! Read it out!

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:52.350
Okay!

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.450
<b>Drown with Spica!
—Turbo</b>

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:55.450
"Drown with Spica!"

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:57.790
Is that spelled wrong?

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.560
So they're declaring war on us?

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.830
I guess we'll have to show them 
who's boss at the racetrack.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.870
Exactly. When you're considered 
the top competitors,

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:07.430
you have to work hard 
to maintain that esteem.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:10.500
Which means, Teio, 
as far as your comeback goes—

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:11.470
Trainer...

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:14.970
I want to enter the Spring Tennoushou.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:21.350
My goal is to continue being undefeated.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:26.850
But I don't think that will mean anything 
unless I take on strong competition.

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:27.690
So...

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.910
That'd mean Teio and McQueen...

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:35.180
You guys okay with potentially 
ruining each other's plans?

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:37.840
I gladly accept the challenge.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:41.830
I expected to race against you someday.

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:44.150
There's no problem, is there, Trainer-san?

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:45.280
Are you two serious?

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:47.150
I'm gonna be the one who achieves her goal.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:49.270
Because I'm not gonna lose 
to you either, McQueen!

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:52.320
And I have no intention of 
allowing you to win, Teio.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:54.300
I will win a consecutive Tennoushou!

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.580
Have it your way.

00:08:55.580 --> 00:09:00.050
In that case, Teio's gonna be running 
in the Osaka Hai before the Tennoushou.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:00.890
Yeah!

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:04.650
And before the Tennoushou, McQueen, 
you need to take on the Hanshin Daishoten.

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:05.850
Understood.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:08.480
I expect both of you to give 
this everything you've got!

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.570
Right!

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:11.920
And don't go telling anyone about this yet.

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:12.280
Got it.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:14.490
I got it, all right!

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.520
Everyone is going to know now.

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:17.580
Man...

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:20.570
A race between members of Spica, huh?

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:26.960
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:26.960
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.460
<b>Teio VS McQueen</b>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.460
<b>Teio VS McQueen</b>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.460
<b>Teio VS McQueen</b>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.460
<b>Teio VS McQueen</b>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.460
<b>Teio VS McQueen</b>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.460
<b>Teio
VS
McQueen</b>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.460
<b>Teio VS McQueen</b>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.460
<b>Drown with Spica!
—Turbo</b>

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.340
<b>TEIO AND MCQUEEN RACING AGAINST EACH OTHER!?</b>

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:35.530
<i>The undefeated horse girl, Tokai Teio,</i>

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:38.340
<i>and the senior-class award-winning 
horse girl, Mejiro McQueen,</i>

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.970
<i>will be clashing at the Tennoushou...</i>

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:43.270
<i>As announced by Team Spica, 
which represents both competitors.</i>

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.650
She's really motivated!

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.020
How many times does that make?

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:53.860
Looking good, McQueen!

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.400
<b>Goal</b>

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.920
Increase your pace a bit more!

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:02.180
Damn, that's a long stretch!

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:04.330
Teio!

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.080
Don't get sloppy with your form!

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:08.750
I know!

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:19.050
<b>Goal</b>

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:25.190
That wasn't hard at all!

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:27.230
All too easy, frankly.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:32.980
<b><u>Down with</u> Spica!
Strategy Meeting</b>

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:32.980
Now, then, it's time for 
today's strategy meeting.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.180
Yeah!

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:35.530
Yeah...

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:39.510
Our subject today: How do 
we avoid losing to Spica?

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:41.740
Yes, Twin Turbo-san?

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:42.860
We come in first place!

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.960
True, yes, but what else?

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:46.510
Uh... don't come in second!

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:47.780
Does that mean third is fine?

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:49.020
We can also avoid racing them!

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:50.500
We won't lose that way, 
but we also won't win!

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:51.960
There's also running hard!

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.000
I guess that works, if it helps you win.

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:56.130
But at the last Arima Kinen...

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:59.130
Number 12, Twin Turbo, is setting 
a fast early pace, like she said.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:59.130
<b>Twin Turbo</b>

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:01.470
<i>I've got this! I've got this!</i>

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:06.550
And McQueen shocks us all 
by coming in second place!

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:05.870
<b>Daitaku Helios</b>

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.500
It just didn't kick in that time!

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.440
What didn't?

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:19.580
What've you been looking at, Ikuno?

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:22.660
Ikuno's running against 
Teio at the Osaka Hai.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:24.470
Tokai Teio...

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:29.160
I'll analyze every aspect of her racing,
 and find a way to beat her.

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:32.020
We should work hard, too!

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.420
Yeah! This calls for more meetings!

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:34.780
Yeah!

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:37.670
Um... you could train instead 
of having meetings.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:40.090
Honey, honey, honey!

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:43.530
When I get a taste of that honey...

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:45.490
Is that...

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:48.840
Here you go. Soft, light, 
and easy on the honey.

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:50.050
McQueen?

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:52.190
That'll be 1,000 yen.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:53.830
What a coincidence.

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:55.330
Yeah, I guess so.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:01.030
So good!

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:04.340
McQueen, you must've been 
training late today, huh?

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:07.290
I could ask you the same thing. You're sure 
you're not overworking yourself?

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:08.780
Right back at you.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:13.780
I must say, it's been quite a while 
since I walked home with you.

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:15.160
It has?

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:19.050
When I first met you, I remember you 
following me around quite a bit.

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:22.000
You were just being too self-conscious.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.840
It's been that way ever 
since the entrance ceremony.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.180
<b>Entrance Ceremony</b>

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:33.650
Is she the one everyone's talking about?

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:34.940
Tokai Teio-san?

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.270
Yeah! She's supposed to be really fast.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:39.120
Let's all have a good time here!

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:54.080
It's a pleasure to be attending 
school with all of you.

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:58.880
You can tell she's from the Mejiro family.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:00.950
And she's supposed to be a great racer, too.

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.930
She's pretty cool!

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:08.300
New students are always united 
in their thoughts and desires,

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:10.320
while each having their distinct resolve,

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:15.640
which I hope will be a source of 
boundless determination for all of you.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.020
Congratulations on your enrollment.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.670
That's the Prez for you!

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:24.900
And now, representing the new class...

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:26.950
An address from Mejiro McQueen-san.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:29.780
Huh? It's the girl from before.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:36.010
As of today, we horse girls have 
become students at Tracen Academy,

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:40.820
where our new lives will begin, 
like the budding of cherry blossoms.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:43.410
As we dedicate ourselves to our 
daily learning and training,

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:48.050
we will now be running the same 
halls as our great forebears....

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:48.050
She's trying to show off 
in front of the Prez!

00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:56.900
McQueen, that's quite the time you managed!

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:59.060
Yes, naturally.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:02.360
That was incredible, Teio!

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:07.860
Impressive.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:09.870
You want to hang out before heading home?

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:12.480
Yeah! I could really go for some steak!

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:13.980
Gotta be steak!

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:41.520
Would you stop already?

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.770
Could you please put an end to this?

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:45.430
Enough!

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:46.860
No more!

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.150
Ow, ow, ow...

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:55.290
O-Oh, you're from the class next door.

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.040
Wh-What a coincidence.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.700
Y-Yes, it must be.

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:00.790
Were you training this late?

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.310
I-I could ask you the same thing.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:03.170
Yes...

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:06.430
You certainly seem tired! Are you alright?

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:09.880
Nope, I'm fine! I'm curious, 
what's that you're carrying?

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.760
I-It's nothing important!

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.560
I-I see!

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:16.270
Th-That's right.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.390
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.140
<b>The Day After That</b>

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.190
<b>And the Day After That</b>

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:31.140
What a coincidence.

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:32.530
I suppose so.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:40.910
We had quite a string of coincidences 
before joining Spica.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:41.540
Yeah.

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:55.210
The cherry blossoms will be blooming soon.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:56.760
Yep.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:03.960
There's a steady rain today 
at the Hanshin Racecourse,

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:06.190
casting a dark pall over the track.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:10.070
This is the first race of the year for our 
most popular competitor, Mejiro McQueen.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:11.420
It should be an interesting one.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:12.380
McQueen!

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:17.330
The rain is nasty today. 
Be careful of the mud, all right?

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.770
You needn't warn me, I assure you.

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:23.220
It was raining during the fall Tennoushou 
last year as well, wasn't it?

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:24.050
You nervous?

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:26.670
Hardly. If anything, I'm glad.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:28.970
Things are different now.

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:32.110
I intend to run hard enough 
to blow the rain away.

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:44.030
There are only six running in this race?

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:47.910
I guess it's only natural, 
with how strong McQueen looks lately.

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:50.310
They've all got McQueen marked.

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:51.910
It's practically five-on-one.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:53.940
You got this, McQueen!

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.810
Where are you going, Teio-san?

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:03.510
I'm gonna just check out the course 
for when I run in the Osaka Hai.

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:07.710
Good luck, McQueen-san!

00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:10.480
Teio-san's here!

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:12.830
Teio-san!

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.840
Kita-chan! We're here to 
root for McQueen-san today!

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:18.250
The horse girls have finished their warm-ups,
 and are headed to the gate.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:17.400
Okay.

00:17:33.730 --> 00:17:36.560
Well! Guess I was worried for nothing.

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:37.860
Teio?

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:40.010
Cheering from beside the course today?

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:42.480
Nope! Just wanted to get a good look at it.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:46.530
You must be awfully confident, 
worrying about me.

00:17:46.530 --> 00:17:47.620
I could say the same to you!

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:49.920
I hope you're all right with 
me getting ahead of you,

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.200
winning this race and all.

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:52.450
Knock yourself out!

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:56.350
Just be sure to watch when I win the 
Osaka Hai. Because I will win it!

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:18.120
The horse girls are at the gate.

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:21.250
As the rain falls on them, 
they wait for the start.

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:27.080
<i>Even if they all come after me...
 I'll accept the challenge.</i>

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.000
<i>We can do this!</i>

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.750
The Hanshin Daishoten, 
a course of 3,000 meters...

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:33.380
has just begun!

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:39.380
At 3,000 meters, this is a long 
race with a small roster!

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.910
It opens things up for 
some interesting tactics!

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:43.640
All right, that's a good start!

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:48.250
They're turning the third 
corner of the first lap.

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:51.770
With the persistent rain, the track 
is likely to be on the heavy side.

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:54.770
<i>I need to make sure to take every step 
steadily and securely to stay on my feet!</i>

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:58.780
<i>If I can maintain my racing style, 
no one should be able to beat me!</i>

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.780
<i>Just like this! Just like this!</i>

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:02.200
The racers are now through the fourth corner

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:04.700
and entering the home 
stretch of the first lap.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.230
Go, McQueen!

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:07.200
Go!

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:09.310
Even in this heavy rain, there are 
a lot of spectators here today

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:12.780
rooting for these horse girls, 
including Mejiro McQueen!

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:13.920
Wow! They're all secure in their positions!

00:19:12.780 --> 00:19:15.210
Now, all six competitors 
have formed up again!

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.210
McQueen-san!

00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:19.470
McQueen, who is aiming to win the 
spring Tennoushou, is currently in third place!

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:21.590
She's in a good position, and staying steady.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:27.550
And right behind Mejiro McQueen, 
not giving an inch, is #5, Kania Curation!

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:31.560
She's positioned behind McQueen, 
ready to make her move at any moment!

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:30.970
Things are looking good.

00:19:30.970 --> 00:19:33.630
Of course they are. 
It's McQueen who's running.

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:35.190
I guess you're right.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:37.140
I thought they'd be coming after her harder!

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:39.190
But at this rate, it should be no problem.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.700
They've entered the second lap.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:44.440
Kania Curation is moving 
up from behind McQueen!

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:46.030
<i>All right, it looks like I can do this!</i>

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:46.800
<i>I can do this! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:47.910
<i>I can do this! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:49.570
<i>I can do this! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:50.250
<i>I can do this! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.500
What's this?!

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:54.530
It looks like the other horse girls are 
all starting to close in on McQueen!

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:52.560
<i>I can do this! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:53.170
<i>I can do this! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:53.790
<i>I can do this! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:54.530
<i>I can do this! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:55.250
<i>I can do this! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:19:56.070 --> 00:19:57.750
<i>This is quite a bit of pressure.</i>

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.480
They've all got her marked!

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:00.470
McQueen-san...

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:02.790
You just had to jinx it, didn't you?

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:04.800
You're the one who brought it up!

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:05.760
Go!

00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:09.270
They've rounded the third corner, 
and are entering the fourth!

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:13.390
<i>From here, I can catch her!</i>

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:14.650
<i>I can catch her!{repeat as necessary}</i>

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:15.900
<i>I can catch her!{repeat as necessary}</i>

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:17.400
<i>I can catch her!{repeat as necessary}</i>

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:21.980
<i>I can totally do this!</i>

00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:24.290
<i>I can catch her!</i>

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:25.030
Here we go.

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:27.710
And McQueen makes her move!
 She's going for it!

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:29.520
Mejiro McQueen has started her spurt!

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:31.420
She's gaining distance 
on the other horse girls!

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:32.010
Wha—?!

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:33.710
Go for it, McQueen!

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:34.960
Wow!

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:38.100
They're on the last stretch, 
and McQueen has quickly taken the lead!

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:41.170
But at the same time, 
Kania Curation is moving in behind her!

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:45.430
Are we looking at a contest between
 Mejiro McQueen and Kania Curation?!

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:47.930
<i>Not yet... Not yet...</i>

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:50.560
<i>This is where... This is where...</i>

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.980
<i>I-I can't—!</i>

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:57.100
We are not! This is not the 
showdown it looked like!

00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:59.110
Mejiro McQueen has gained 
a lead and keeps going!

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.830
Mejiro McQueen is dashing 
toward another confrontation

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:02.880
at the spring Tennoushou!

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:04.070
She's amazing!

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:04.070
Her lead is only getting bigger!

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:06.120
This is completely one-sided!

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:09.490
And Mejiro McQueen clears the goal!

00:21:14.190 --> 00:21:17.500
She's left the second place 
finish five lengths behind her!

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.430
Hell yeah!

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:19.880
She did it!

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.950
McQueen-san!

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:26.410
I'm really looking forward 
to her race with Teio.

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:27.660
Tell me about it!

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:30.130
But I think McQueen's got the edge.

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:32.520
I mean, after the way she blew the 
second place runner away, yeah!

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:36.260
I thought so, too! You've got a great eye!

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:38.320
Teio-san's better, though.

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:39.880
No, McQueen-san!

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:41.150
Teio-san!

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.780
McQueen really is tough.

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:51.720
Teio?

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:54.750
Trainer, I'm going to impress
you at the Osaka Hai.

00:21:55.470 --> 00:21:56.180
Do it!

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:05.560
<i>It's your turn next.</i>

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:08.790
<i>I'm not gonna lose, either.</i>

00:23:36.900 --> 00:23:39.600
Everyone has been waiting for her return.

00:23:39.970 --> 00:23:44.480
The Twin Crown horse girl is now making 
her presence felt at the Osaka Hai!

00:23:45.120 --> 00:23:47.680
In the second bracket, #2, 
the most anticipated competitor...

00:23:48.730 --> 00:23:50.540
Tokai Teio!
